  "worked_solution": "In the model, we have $\\frac{3}{4}$ on the left.\n\nSince we need to multiply by $\\frac{4}{5}$, we split the whole into $5$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $4$ of the parts remain shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/b40e2ec88f84324a67fed2df4726425e42971ba87c64714ba6521659d078495e.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{12}{20}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore, the missing picture is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/bcfd098d20bdaeaf4aaef601bf185f38bcfedec713e23b82d726bba8d08e75ea.png)",
